{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "tz_92",
  "notes": "Boot tz_92 from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released), navigate the service menu to T.16 CLOCK TEST (the 9.2 ROM inserts T.14 LAMP ROW/COLUMN and T.15 DIP SW. TEST, so the 1993 manual's T.14 is T.16 here), then start and stop each of the four clock operations in turn (the manual lists Clock Forward Slow, Clock Forward Fast, Clock Reverse Slow and Clock Reverse Fast, selected with service Up and started/stopped with Enter). Every snapshot records the DMD, whose top line names the current operation, and the output transitions show which public custom solenoid (56 or 57, the 8-driver board's drives 42 and 43) the ROM holds on for each named operation.",
